input.command:
cd /Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/cli/cli-dispatch-jurisdiction; python3 - <<'PYEOF'
p='cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go'
s=open(p).read()
a='''		// huh's accessible runner ignores hide funcs and never evaluates an
		// OptionsFunc, so dynamic groups cannot work there: the jurisdiction
		// picker is skipped (--jurisdiction remains the way to scope) and the
		// repo list is resolved up front, unscoped.
		repoPicker.Options(buildDispatchRepoOptions(loadScope().reposIn(""))...)'''
b='''		// huh's accessible runner ignores hide funcs and never evaluates an
		// OptionsFunc, so dynamic groups cannot work there: the jurisdiction
		// picker is skipped (--jurisdiction remains the way to scope) and the
		// repo list is resolved up front with EVERY offerable repo — not
		// reposIn(""), which is the unplaced bucket once placements are known.
		repoPicker.Options(buildDispatchRepoOptions(loadScope().repos)...)'''
if a not in s: raise SystemExit("no match")
open(p,'w').write(s.replace(a,b,1))
PYEOF
gofmt -l cmd/entire/cli; go build ./... && go test -race ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run 'Dispatch|Jurisdiction|Wizard' 2>&1 | grep -v INFO | tail -2 && mise run lint 2>&1 | grep '\[lint:go\] [0-9]* issues' && git add -A cmd/entire/cli && git commit -q -m "dispatch: accessible wizard offers every repo, not the unplaced bucket

reposIn(\"\") became the home-unknown/unplaced bucket once placements are
known, so the accessible-mode repo picker (which cannot scope by
jurisdiction) hid mirrored repos. Offer the whole catalogue there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED" && git push 2>&1 | tail -1 && git log --oneline -1

